FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://bank-system.apiary.io

# Bank Saving System API
The Bank Saving System API allows client applications to manage customers, deposito types, accounts, and transactions stored in a MySQL database. All responses follow a consistent JSON envelope using the `success` flag and either `data` or `message`.

## Authentication
This example API does not implement authentication. All endpoints are open for demonstration purposes.

# Group Customers

## Customers Collection [/customers]

### List Customers [GET]
Retrieve the full list of customers.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": [
                { "id": 1, "name": "John Doe" },
                { "id": 2, "name": "Jane Smith" }
            ]
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Create Customer [POST]
Create a new customer.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "name": "John Doe"
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 3,
                "name": "John Doe"
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Customer name is required"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

## Customer Resource [/customers/{id}]
+ Parameters
    + id: 1 (number, required) - Customer identifier.

### Get Customer by ID [GET]
Retrieve a single customer.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1,
                "name": "John Doe"
            }
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Customer not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Update Customer [PUT]
Update an existing customer's name.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "name": "Updated Name"
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1,
                "name": "Updated Name"
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Customer name is required"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Customer not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Delete Customer [DELETE]
Remove a customer. Deletion is prevented when accounts exist for the customer.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1
            },
            "message": "Customer deleted"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Cannot delete customer with existing accounts"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Customer not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

# Group Accounts

## Accounts Collection [/accounts]

### List Accounts [GET]
Retrieve the list of accounts along with customer and deposito type information.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": [
                {
                    "id": 1,
                    "customer_id": 1,
                    "customer_name": "John Doe",
                    "deposito_type_id": 2,
                    "deposito_type_name": "Deposito Gold",
                    "yearly_return": 7.0,
                    "balance": 500000.00
                }
            ]
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Create Account [POST]
Create a new account. Customer and deposito type must exist.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "customer_id": 1,
                "deposito_type_id": 2,
                "balance": 0
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 5,
                "customer_id": 1,
                "customer_name": "John Doe",
                "deposito_type_id": 2,
                "deposito_type_name": "Deposito Gold",
                "yearly_return": 7.0,
                "balance": 0.00
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Balance must be a non-negative number"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Deposito type not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

## Account Resource [/accounts/{id}]
+ Parameters
    + id: 1 (number, required) - Account identifier.

### Get Account by ID [GET]
Retrieve details for a single account.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1,
                "customer_id": 1,
                "customer_name": "John Doe",
                "deposito_type_id": 2,
                "deposito_type_name": "Deposito Gold",
                "yearly_return": 7.0,
                "balance": 500000.00
            }
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Account not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Update Account [PUT]
Update an account's deposito type.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "deposito_type_id": 3
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1,
                "customer_id": 1,
                "customer_name": "John Doe",
                "deposito_type_id": 3,
                "deposito_type_name": "Deposito Platinum",
                "yearly_return": 8.0,
                "balance": 500000.00
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Invalid deposito_type_id"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Account not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Delete Account [DELETE]
Delete an account. Accounts with transactions cannot be deleted.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1
            },
            "message": "Account deleted"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Cannot delete account with existing transactions"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Account not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

# Group Deposito Types

## Deposito Types Collection [/deposito-types]

### List Deposito Types [GET]
Retrieve all deposito types.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": [
                { "id": 1, "name": "Deposito Silver", "yearly_return": 3.5 },
                { "id": 2, "name": "Deposito Gold", "yearly_return": 7.0 }
            ]
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Create Deposito Type [POST]
Create a new deposito type.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "name": "Deposito Gold",
                "yearly_return": 7.0
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 4,
                "name": "Deposito Gold",
                "yearly_return": 7.0
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "yearly_return must be a number"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

## Deposito Type Resource [/deposito-types/{id}]
+ Parameters
    + id: 1 (number, required) - Deposito type identifier.

### Get Deposito Type by ID [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1,
                "name": "Deposito Silver",
                "yearly_return": 3.5
            }
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Deposito type not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Update Deposito Type [PUT]

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "name": "Deposito Platinum",
                "yearly_return": 8.0
            }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1,
                "name": "Deposito Platinum",
                "yearly_return": 8.0
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Deposito type name is required"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Deposito type not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

### Delete Deposito Type [DELETE]
Prevent deletion when the deposito type is referenced by accounts.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "id": 1
            },
            "message": "Deposito type deleted"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Cannot delete deposito type that is used by existing accounts"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Deposito type not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

# Group Transactions & Balance

## Deposit Resource [/accounts/{id}/deposit]
+ Parameters
    + id: 1 (number, required) - Account identifier.

### Deposit to Account [POST]
Add funds to an account and create a deposit transaction.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "amount": 100000.00,
                "date": "2025-12-01"
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "account": {
                    "id": 1,
                    "customer_id": 1,
                    "deposito_type_id": 2,
                    "balance": 600000.00,
                    "customer_name": "John Doe",
                    "deposito_type_name": "Deposito Gold",
                    "yearly_return": 7.0
                },
                "transaction": {
                    "id": 15,
                    "account_id": 1,
                    "type": "deposit",
                    "amount": 100000.00,
                    "date": "2025-12-01"
                }
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Amount must be greater than zero"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Account not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

## Withdraw Resource [/accounts/{id}/withdraw]
+ Parameters
    + id: 1 (number, required) - Account identifier.

### Withdraw from Account [POST]
Withdraw funds and create a withdraw transaction.

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

            Content-Type: application/json

    + Body

            {
                "amount": 50000.00,
                "date": "2025-12-02"
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "account": {
                    "id": 1,
                    "customer_id": 1,
                    "deposito_type_id": 2,
                    "balance": 450000.00,
                    "customer_name": "John Doe",
                    "deposito_type_name": "Deposito Gold",
                    "yearly_return": 7.0
                },
                "transaction": {
                    "id": 16,
                    "account_id": 1,
                    "type": "withdraw",
                    "amount": 50000.00,
                    "date": "2025-12-02"
                }
            }
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Insufficient balance"
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Account not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }

## Ending Balance Resource [/accounts/{id}/calculate-ending-balance]
+ Parameters
    + id: 1 (number, required) - Account identifier.

### Calculate Ending Balance [GET]
Return the projected ending balance using current balance, monthly return (yearly_return / 12 / 100), and a hardcoded 12-month period.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "success": true,
            "data": {
                "account_id": 1,
                "starting_balance": 1000000.00,
                "months": 12,
                "monthly_return": 0.005,
                "ending_balance": 1060000.00
            }
        }

+ Response 404 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Account not found"
        }

+ Response 500 (application/json)

        {
            "success": false,
            "message": "Internal server error"
        }
